# Contributor workflow

See [README.md](README.md) and the
[Consensys documentation contribution guidelines](https://docs-template.consensys.com/)
for baseline workflow.

## Sidebars

Sidebars are configured in `sidebars.js`.
Most sections are autogenerated from filesystem structure.

Use `_category_.json`, `sidebar_position`, and `sidebar_label` to control ordering and labels.

## Redirects

Every deleted, renamed, or moved page should have redirect coverage:

- Add or update redirect entries in `docusaurus.config.js` under `@docusaurus/plugin-client-redirects`.
- Update `vercel.json` when versioned route behavior also needs adjustment.

Broken links fail builds (`onBrokenLinks: "throw"`).

## Factual accuracy

Do not invent CLI flags, API fields, defaults, or operational behavior.
If uncertain, flag the uncertainty for review.

## Issue intake

Issue templates live in `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`.
When issue context is sparse, verify behavior from source materials before updating docs.

## Images

Store doc images in `static/img/` and link them with site paths (for example, `/img/<file-name>`).

## Versioning and agent outputs

`lastVersion` in `docusaurus.config.js` is the single source of truth for the stable version.
Two consumers read it:

- The `docsDir` assignment at the end of `docusaurus.config.js`, which points
  `docusaurus-plugin-llms` at `versioned_docs/version-<stable>/`.
- `scripts/copy-md-to-build.js`, which matches the literal with a regex.

Keep `lastVersion` a literal string. Moving it into a shared constant or variable breaks that
regex, which then silently falls back to the first entry in `versions.json` — wrong in the window
after a version is frozen but before `lastVersion` is bumped.

Freezing a version and bumping `lastVersion` is all a release needs; the agent outputs follow.

The REST operation pages are generated at build time. `npm start` and `npm run build` run
`gen-api-docs`, which runs `scripts/fetch-openapi-specs.js` to fetch and bundle the OpenAPI specs
from the Web3Signer tag that matches `lastVersion`, then writes `docs/reference/api/eth1` and
`eth2`. The specs and pages are gitignored, and there is no spec sync workflow: bumping
`lastVersion` is what moves the API reference to a new release. Set `WEB3SIGNER_SPEC_REF` to
preview another tag, branch, or commit. The reference is not versioned.
The command then links `eth1` and `eth2` inside every `versioned_docs/version-*/reference/api/`
directory at those source folders, so stable and development serve the same API pages. A later
`docs:version` copies `docs/` into the new snapshot, including a copy of the API folders. Run
`npm run gen-api-docs` again after the freeze so those copies become links, and commit the links
rather than the generated pages. The new snapshot still picks up the sidebar groups from `sidebars.js`.

`scripts/api-markdown-to-build.js` writes one `.md` file per operation into the build, for both
trees. Those files are not committed. On an API page, Copy page and View as Markdown read that
file.

`scripts/copy-md-to-build.js` copies the stable home page to `build/index.md` and rewrites the
`llms.txt` home page entry to `/index.md`.
That is deliberate: `docusaurus-plugin-llms` discards the `slug: /` frontmatter on the home page
and emits a URL that does not resolve. Do not remove the rewrite, and do not add a
`static/index.md`. Contributors edit the docs home page only.

## Keep rule files current

If you change documentation structure, naming, or formatting conventions, update the matching
`.cursor/rules/` file in the same PR so AI guidance does not go stale.

## CI linting and verification

Before requesting review:

- Run local preview with `npm start`.
- Run lint checks used by CI.
- Verify redirects and links.

CI includes docs linting, markdown linting, link checks, and builds.
